## gstack

Required install, NOT redistributed (since ytstack 0.3.0; it was a git
subtree at vendor/gstack/ from 0.1.x to 0.2.0). Source repository:
<https://github.com/garrytan/gstack>

License: MIT (upstream). ytstack does not ship any gstack file. Six ytstack
skills (skills/office-hours/, skills/plan-ceo-review/, skills/plan-eng-review/,
skills/retro/, skills/ship/, skills/document-release/)
detect a gstack installation under ~/.claude/skills/gstack (tested against
v1.96.0.0, requires bun >= 1.4.2) and invoke its skills through the Skill tool.

Attribution: gstack originates from Garry Tan's work, shaped around YC-style
product and engineering review patterns. ytstack also adopted several of its
UX conventions (AskUserQuestion format, cascading binary questions,
outcome framing) in its own prose; see docs/methodology.md.

